Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: balance the TB371FC headless OF node reference

The TB371FC headless fallback uses of_find_node_with_property() as a
Boolean. The lookup returns a referenced node, so each successful lookup
leaks that reference.

Move only the Boolean lookup into a helper and release the reference
before returning its presence. Keep the existing short-circuit order,
whole-tree property lookup and device predicate unchanged. This does not
change headless registration, IOMMU selection or the global-page-table
experiment.

Apply to official Linux v6.12.114 after
experimental/community-handoff/reference/kernel-6.12.114/working-tree.patch.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
@@ -108,6 +108,18 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static bool tb371fc_has_headless_gpu(void)
+{
+	struct device_node *np;
+	bool found;
+
+	np = of_find_node_with_property(NULL, "tb371fc,headless-gpu");
+	found = np != NULL;
+	of_node_put(np);
+
+	return found;
+}
+
 bool msm_use_mmu(struct drm_device *dev)
 {
 	struct msm_drm_private *priv = dev->dev_private;
@@ -123,7 +135,7 @@
 		device_iommu_mapped(dev->dev) ||
 		device_iommu_mapped(dev->dev->parent) ||
 		(!dev->dev->of_node &&
-		 of_find_node_with_property(NULL, "tb371fc,headless-gpu"));
+		 tb371fc_has_headless_gpu());
 }
 
 static int msm_init_vram(struct drm_device *dev)
